module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.CoherentStackNoetherianDescent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.NumericalDirectImagePerfect
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.QuotFunctorAlgebraicSpaceBounded
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.QuotHilbertPolynomial
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.QuotNumericalCondition
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.TwistedEulerFiniteProjectiveModel

/-!
# `Quot^P_{F/X/B}` is a flat closed subspace of `Quot_{F/X/B}` (Stacks 0DP6)

Let `f : X ⟶ B` be a separated morphism of algebraic spaces of finite presentation, `F` a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module, `I` a set, `E_i ∈ D(𝒪_X)` perfect for `i ∈ I` and `P : I → ℤ`.
Remark 0DP6 forms the fibre product

```
Quot^P_{F/X/B} ⟶ Coh^P_{X/B}
      ↓               ↓
Quot_{F/X/B}   ⟶ Coh_{X/B}
```

(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation.numericalQuot`) and asserts that it defines an algebraic
space, and that its left vertical arrow is a flat closed immersion, which is an open and closed
immersion if `I` is finite, or `B` is locally Noetherian, or `I = ℤ` and `E_i = 𝓛^{⊗ i}` for an
invertible `𝒪_X`-module `𝓛`.

Since `Coh^P_{X/B}` is a full subcategory of `Coh_{X/B}` stable under its morphisms, the fibre
product is the subfunctor `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation.numericalQuotSubspace` of the
Quot presheaf of the quotients `F_T ⟶ 𝒬` whose object `(T, 𝒬)` of `Coh_{X/B}` lies in
`Coh^P_{X/B}`.  Each assertion is the base change along `Quot_{F/X/B} ⟶ Coh_{X/B}` of the
corresponding assertion about `Coh^P_{X/B} ⊆ Coh_{X/B}` (Lemma 0DND, Example 0DNF).

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation.numericalQuotSubspace`: `Quot^P_{F/X/B}` as a subfunctor
  of the Quot presheaf.

## Main results

All of these live in the namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation`.

* `mem_numericalQuotSubspace_iff`: a quotient lies in
  `Quot^P_{F/X/B}` exactly when its object of `Coh_{X/B}` lies in `Coh^P_{X/B}`.
* `numericalQuotToQuot_fullyFaithful_and_mem_numericalQuotSubspace_iff`:
  the subfunctor is the fibre product of the remark.
* `relative_closedImmersion_flat_numericalQuotSubspace_ι`:
  `Quot^P_{F/X/B} ⟶ Quot_{F/X/B}` is a flat closed immersion.
* `relative_openImmersion_closedImmersion_numericalQuotSubspace_ι_of_finite`
  and
  `relative_openImmersion_closedImmersion_numericalQuotSubspace_ι_of_isLocallyNoetherian`:
  it is an open and closed immersion if `I` is finite or `B` is locally Noetherian.
* `relative_openImmersion_closedImmersion_hilbertPolynomialQuot_ι`:
  for `I = ℤ` and `E_i = 𝓛^{⊗ i}`, the subfunctor `Quot^{P, 𝓛}_{F/X/B}` of the quotients with
  Hilbert polynomial `P` is an open and closed subspace.
* `isAlgebraicSpace_subfunctorModel_numericalQuotSubspace`:
  `Quot^P_{F/X/B}` is an algebraic space, for `F` étale-locally generated by fewer sections than
  the cutoff of the site.

## Implementation notes

A quotient is recorded by a subobject, so the Quot presheaf and its subfunctors take values one
universe above the schemes of the site; "`Quot^P_{F/X/B}` is an algebraic space" is said of its
models in the universe of the site (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation.SubfunctorModel`), and
"the left vertical arrow is a flat closed immersion" is the representability of the inclusion by
flat closed immersions of schemes along `CategoryTheory.uliftYoneda`.

On a big fppf site, whose schemes are bounded in size by a cutoff `κ`, the algebraicity of
`Quot^P_{F/X/B}` fails for an arbitrary quasi-coherent `F`: for the empty index set
`Quot^P_{F/X/B} = Quot_{F/X/B}`, and the Quot functor of a free module of
rank `κ + 1` over the spectrum of a separably closed field has too many points to be an
algebraic space.  The algebraicity is therefore stated for `F` étale-locally generated by fewer
than `μ` sections for some `μ` below the cutoff, which every `F` of finite type is.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DP6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DP6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DNC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DNC)
